      "side": 1,
      "message": "Thanks Pavan, I found the cycle. On Android, VideoRtpSession::startSender() holds the session mutex while getVideoInput() creates the VideoInput, which emits StartCapture synchronously; HardwareServiceImpl.startCapture() then calls JamiService.getCallDetails(), which takes the call mutex (Call::getState()). Patch set 1 took the call mutex and then the session mutex in forceKeyFrame(), so a picture_fast_update from the peer arriving while startAllMedia() starts our video sender deadlocked both threads. Patch set 2 copies the video sessions under the call mutex and forces the keyframes once it is released, and runs on the I/O pool like setRotation(). If your trace showed another cycle, could you share it?",
